# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in `openclaw.json`, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP klientkontrakt:** Med Home Assistant implementert, rollen erklærer MCP-klientsiden av plattformen kontrakt som en intern streamingable-HTTP klient med en lesebeskyttet verktøypolicy. MCP-serverlisten bor i `openclaw.json`, Ikke i beholdermiljøet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` registry under an `infinito:` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider's declared allowlist. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` plus an `HTTP_DENY_LIST` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
msgstr "**MCP klientkontrakt:** Med en MCP-server utplassert ved siden av den, erklærer rollen MCP klientsiden av plattformen kontrakt som en intern streamingable-HTTP klient med en skrivebeskyttet verktøypolicy. Utplasseringen registrerer alle oppdagede leverandører i instansnivå `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` Register under et `infinito:` navn, lagrer bæreren som en kryptert `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, godkjenner hver oppføring og sammenligner det oppdaget verktøyet mot leverandørens erklærte tillateliste. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` Fester distribusjonen til URL-baserte MCP-servere, slik at ingen flyt kan gyte en lokal stdio-kommando. Å nå en MCP-server som løser URL i containernettverket krever `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` pluss en `HTTP_DENY_LIST` som holder loopback og cloud-metadata-adresser nektet; begge gjøres bare mens MCP-servere blir oppdaget, og distribusjonen beviser at listen er live ved å peke på en kastaway-oppføring på hver nektet adresse. En administrert Agentflow fixtur kaller et enkelt navngitt verktøy med faste argumenter og utføres på hver distribusjon. Å koble en leverandør til en flyt av egen forblir et operatørsteg."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level ``/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`` registry under an ``infinito:`` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted ``CUSTOM_HEADERS`` ``authConfig``, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider’s declared allowlist. ``CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse`` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires ``HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false`` plus an ``HTTP_DENY_LIST`` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
