# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects `/` to the public `/discover` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only `/login` binds the SSO directive (see the note in [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga's SSO button. Taiga's AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local `test-login-oidc.js` and `test-login-native.js` specs, which enter at `/login` and log out through Taiga's own control."
msgstr "Taiga omdirigerer `/` til offentligheten `/discover` showcase, som gjør en bare Login-lenke, men ikke OIDC-inngangspunkt; bare `/login` binder SSO-direktivet (Se noten i [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). De delte personene alltid inn på nettstedet rot, slik at de aldri kan nå TaigaSSO-knappen. Taigas AngularJS skall eksponerer også utlogging bare gjennom `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` direktiver som den generiske utloggingshjelperen i appen ikke kan aktivere. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) Derfor erklærer `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` og `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; Ekvivalente reiser drives av rolle-lokale `test-login-oidc.js` og `test-login-native.js` Spesifikasjoner som går inn i `/login` Logg ut gjennom Taigaegen kontroll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects ``/`` to the public ``/discover`` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only ``/login`` binds the SSO directive (see the note in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` and log out through Taiga’s own control."
msgstr "Taiga omdirigerer ``/`` til offentligheten ``/discover`` showcase, som gjør en bare Login-lenke, men ikke OIDC-inngangspunkt; bare ``/login`` binder SSO-direktivet (Se noten i ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` Logg ut gjennom Taigaegen kontroll."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (``pacman``). It deploys a ``policies.json`` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
msgstr "Tailored for Arch Linux, denne rollen håndterer installasjonen Firefox bruk av systemets pakkehåndtering (``pacman``). Den distribuerer en ``policies.json`` fil til Firefoxdistribusjonsmappen, som sikrer at kritiske utvidelser installeres automatisk via Firefox Forretningspolitikk."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tailored for Arch Linux, this role handles the installation of Firefox using the system’s package manager (`pacman`). It deploys a `policies.json` file to Firefox’s distribution directory, ensuring that critical extensions are automatically installed via Firefox Enterprise Policies."
