# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the log carries the matrix-deploy round/pass markers, the result is segmented (one block of records per variant round + pass). Otherwise a single combined block is returned. Runtime rows are read from the ``ROLES RECAP`` sections only (never ``TASKS RECAP``, whose role-less task rows would double-count); a log without any recap header falls back to reading every profile-shaped line. The recap ``total`` line survives as the ``total`` row so consumers can cross-check the parsed sum. Per-host task results (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) accumulate into each record's ``hosts`` field; delegation targets (``[host -> other]``) count for the source host. Raises FileNotFoundError when the log is absent (the caller turns that into a hard failure)."
msgstr "Når loggen bærer matrise-demploy runde/pass markører, er resultatet segmentert (en blokk av poster per variant runde + pass). Ellers returneres en enkelt kombinert blokk. Runtime rader leses fra ``ROLES RECAP`` kun seksjoner (Aldri ``TASKS RECAP``, hvis rolleløse oppgaverader ville dobbelttalt); en logg uten noe recap-hode faller tilbake til å lese hver profilformet linje. Recap ``total`` linje overlever som ``total`` ro slik at forbrukere kan krysse sjekk den tolkede summen. Per-host oppgaveresultater (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` overskrift) samles inn i hver rekord ``hosts`` felt; delegeringsmål (``[host -> other]``) teller for kildeværten. Løfter filenNotFoundError når loggen er fraværende (Ringeren gjør det til en hard feil).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Når Oauth2-proxy SSO smak er aktiv, Snipe-IT's morsmål ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` er aktivert via ``Setting`` modell (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx porter ``/login`` gjennom Oauth2-proxy/Keycloak og injiserer den verifiserte ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, som Snipe-IT stemmer mot ``users.username`` (brukeren må forhåndseksistere og aktiveres — synkroniser dem via LDAP) å tegne en innfødt ``snipeit_session``. Besøkende uten en matchende aktivert bruker faller stille gjennom til det normale innloggingsskjemaet (ingen feil). passord/LDAP-innloggingsskjemaet forblir tilgjengelig som en reserve (``login_common_disabled = 0``), og i-app-utloggingen er omdirigert til den sentrale OIDC sluttsession URL."

