# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`RUNNER_COUNT` defaults to `RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS // RUNNER_CPUS` (auto-scaled to hardware). Override explicitly when debugging a specific count."
msgstr "`RUNNER_COUNT` standard til `RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS // RUNNER_CPUS` (automatisk skalert til maskinvare). Overstyr eksplisitt ved feilsøking av et bestemt antall."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`RUNNER_DISTRIBUTION` is **required** and has no default; it is passed automatically by the CLI."
msgstr "`RUNNER_DISTRIBUTION` er **nødvendig** og har ingen standard; den blir overført automatisk av CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`RUNNER_GITHUB_OWNER` and `RUNNER_GITHUB_REPO` resolve from `GITHUB_REPOSITORY_OWNER` / `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` env vars when set (CI context), falling back to `meta/services.yml` for production deploys."
msgstr "`RUNNER_GITHUB_OWNER` og `RUNNER_GITHUB_REPO` Løsning fra `GITHUB_REPOSITORY_OWNER` / `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` env vars når satt (CI-kontekst), faller tilbake til `meta/services.yml` For produksjonsplasser."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`RUNTIME` (`dev`/`act`/`github`) selects which test stages run."
msgstr "`RUNTIME` (`dev`/`act`/`github`) velger hvilke testfaser som kjører."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`RetroArch <https://www.retroarch.com/>`__ is a frontend for emulators, game engines, and media players powered by the `Libretro <https://www.libretro.com/>`__ framework. It supports multiple UI styles including `XMB <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XrossMediaBar>`__ and `Ozone <https://docs.libretro.com/>`__, and provides a unified interface for retro gaming across platforms."
msgstr "`RetroArch <https://www.retroarch.com/>`__ er en frontend for emulatorer, spillmotorer og mediespillere drevet av `Libretro <https://www.libretro.com/>`__ rammeverk. Den støtter flere UI-stiler inkludert `XMB <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XrossMediaBar>`__ og `Ozone <https://docs.libretro.com/>`__, og gir et samlet grensesnitt for retro spill på tvers av plattformer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Roulette Wheel <https://github.com/p-wojt/roulette-wheel>`__ is a Node.js-based front-end application that simulates a roulette wheel in the browser."
msgstr "`Roulette Wheel <https://github.com/p-wojt/roulette-wheel>`__ er en Node.js-basert front-end program som simulerer et roulette hjul i nettleseren."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_ACCESS_KEY_ENCRYPTION` (base64 32 bytes, `head -c32 /dev/urandom | base64`) encrypts stored access keys; `SEMAPHORE_COOKIE_HASH` / `SEMAPHORE_COOKIE_ENCRYPTION` secure sessions."
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_ACCESS_KEY_ENCRYPTION` (base64 32 byte, `head -c32 /dev/urandom | base64`) krypterer lagrede tilgangsnøkler; `SEMAPHORE_COOKIE_HASH` / `SEMAPHORE_COOKIE_ENCRYPTION` trygge økter."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_ADMIN`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_NAME`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_EMAIL` seed the first admin (no setup wizard)."
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_ADMIN`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_NAME`, `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_EMAIL` Seed den første admin (ingen oppsettsveiviser).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_DB_DIALECT` ∈ `bolt` (file at `/var/lib/semaphore`), `mysql`, `postgres`. Postgres uses `SEMAPHORE_DB_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SEMAPHORE_DB`."
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_DB_DIALECT` ∈ `bolt` (fil på `/var/lib/semaphore`), `mysql`, `postgres`. Postgres bruker `SEMAPHORE_DB_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SEMAPHORE_DB`.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_LDAP_ACTIVATED`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_HOST`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_PORT`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_NEEDTLS`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_DN_BIND`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_PASSWORD`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_DN_SEARCH`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_SEARCH_FILTER`, plus attribute mappings (`SEMAPHORE_LDAP_MAPPING_DN/UID/MAIL/CN`)."
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_LDAP_ACTIVATED`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_HOST`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_PORT`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_NEEDTLS`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_DN_BIND`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_PASSWORD`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_DN_SEARCH`, `SEMAPHORE_LDAP_SEARCH_FILTER`, pluss attributtkartlegginger (`SEMAPHORE_LDAP_MAPPING_DN/UID/MAIL/CN`).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_OIDC_PROVIDERS` = JSON map. Per-provider: `display_name`, `provider_url` (issuer), `client_id`, `client_secret`, `redirect_url`. Redirect path is `https://<host>/api/auth/oidc/<provider_id>/redirect`. **Semaphore has native OIDC — no `oauth2-proxy` sidecar needed.**"
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_OIDC_PROVIDERS` = JSON-kart. Per leverandør: `display_name`, `provider_url` (Utsteder), `client_id`, `client_secret`, `redirect_url`. Redirect bane er `https://<host>/api/auth/oidc/<provider_id>/redirect`.. **Semaphore har innfødt OIDC — nei `oauth2-proxy` bil trengs.**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SEMAPHORE_WEB_ROOT` sets the externally-reachable base URL; required for correct OIDC redirects behind `sys-svc-proxy`."
msgstr "`SEMAPHORE_WEB_ROOT` angir den eksternt flyttbare baseadressen; som kreves for riktig OIDC-omdirigeringer bak `sys-svc-proxy`.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SH_APPS_CATALOG_URL` is emptied so the container never fetches the app catalog from github.com. Set it to a self-hosted catalog when one exists."
msgstr "`SH_APPS_CATALOG_URL` er tømt slik at beholderen aldri henter appkatalogen fra github.com. Sett det til en selv-vert katalog når en eksisterer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SH_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is unset — the SPA is same-origin. Needed only if a third-party client should talk to the API."
msgstr "`SH_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` Det er urovekkende — SPA er samme utsagn. Trenger kun dersom en tredjeparts klient bør snakke med API.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SH_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES` is pinned to 4 GiB in `vars/main.yml` so the app's media cap stays inside `services.socialhome.min_storage` (5 GB). Raising one without the other lets the volume outgrow its declared budget."
msgstr "`SH_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES` er festet til 4 GiB i `vars/main.yml` så appens mediehette forblir inne `services.socialhome.min_storage` (5 GB). Å heve den ene uten den andre lar volumet utløpe sitt erklært budsjett."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SSH (Secure Shell) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell>`__ is a cryptographic network protocol for operating network services securely over an unsecured network. The `OpenSSH <https://www.openssh.com/>`__ project provides the reference implementation, including ``ssh-agent`` for managing authentication keys."
msgstr "`SSH (Secure Shell) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell>`__ er en kryptografisk nettverksprotokoll for å betjene nettverkstjenester sikkert over et usikret nettverk. Den `OpenSSH <https://www.openssh.com/>`__ Prosjektet gir referanse implementering, inkludert ``ssh-agent`` for å administrere autentiseringsnøkler."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SYS_SERVICE_RUNNER_STATE` (string): desired state (`started`, `restarted`, ...)"
msgstr "`SYS_SERVICE_RUNNER_STATE` (streng): Ønsket tilstand (`started`, `restarted`,...)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SearXNG <https://docs.searxng.org/>`__ is a metasearch engine. It forwards a query to other search engines and returns the merged result without an account and without a tracking profile."
msgstr "`SearXNG <https://docs.searxng.org/>`__ En metasearchmotor. Den viderefører en spørring til andre søkemotorer og returnerer det sammenslåtte resultatet uten en konto og uten sporingsprofil."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`SeaweedFS <https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs>`__ is a fast distributed storage system for blobs, objects, and files. It exposes an S3-compatible API, so applications store and retrieve objects with standard S3 SDKs and CLIs."
msgstr "`SeaweedFS <https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs>`__ er et raskt distribuert lagringssystem for blobs, objekter og filer. Det avslører en S3-kompatibel API, så programmer lagre og hente objekter med standard S3 SDK og CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Semaphore UI <https://semaphoreui.com/>`__ is a modern web UI and API for running Ansible playbooks, Terraform/OpenTofu plans, and shell scripts on a schedule or on demand. This role deploys the official ```semaphoreui/semaphore`` <https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore>`__ container behind the Infinito.Nexus reverse proxy with central PostgreSQL, native Keycloak OIDC Single Sign-On, and optional LDAP login."
msgstr "`Semaphore UI <https://semaphoreui.com/>`__ En moderne web UI og API For å kjøre Ansible spillebøker, Terraform/OpenTofu planer, og skall skript på en tidsplan eller etterspørsel. Denne rollen distribuerer den offisielle ```semaphoreui/semaphore`` <https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore>`beholder bak Infinito.Nexus omvendt proxy med sentralt PostgreSQL, innfødt Keycloak OIDC Single Logg på og valgfri LDAP-innlogging."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Svc Engine <https://example.com/>`__ is an application."
msgstr "`Svc Engine <https://example.com/>`__ Det er en søknad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Svc Objstore <https://example.com/>`__ is an application."
msgstr "`Svc Objstore <https://example.com/>`__ Det er en søknad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_COMMAND` (default: `npm install --no-fund --no-audit && npx playwright test`)"
msgstr "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_COMMAND` (standard: `npm install --no-fund --no-audit && npx playwright test`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_IMAGE_DISTRO` (default: `noble`)"
msgstr "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_IMAGE_DISTRO` (standard: `noble`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_IMAGE` (resolved in `vars/main.yml` from `meta/services.yml.playwright.image` + `.version` via `lookup('config', 'test-e2e-playwright', 'services.playwright.image|version')`)"
msgstr "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_IMAGE` (Løst i `vars/main.yml` fra `meta/services.yml.playwright.image` + `.version` via `lookup('config', 'test-e2e-playwright', 'services.playwright.image|version')`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_REPORTS_BASE_DIR` (default: `/var/lib/infinito/logs/test-e2e-playwright`)"
msgstr "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_REPORTS_BASE_DIR` (standard: `/var/lib/infinito/logs/test-e2e-playwright`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_STAGE_BASE_DIR` (default: `/tmp/test-e2e-playwright`)"
msgstr "`TEST_E2E_PLAYWRIGHT_STAGE_BASE_DIR` (standard: `/tmp/test-e2e-playwright`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Taiga <https://www.taiga.io/>`__ is a powerful and intuitive open-source project management platform tailored for agile teams. Whether you’re practicing Scrum, Kanban, or a custom hybrid workflow, Taiga offers a rich, customizable environment to plan, track, and collaborate on your projects, without the complexity of enterprise tools or the vendor lock-in of SaaS platforms."
msgstr "`Taiga <https://www.taiga.io/>`__ er en kraftig og intuitiv åpen kildekode prosjektledelse plattform skreddersydd for agile teams. Enten du praktiserer Scrum, Kanban eller en egendefinert hybrid arbeidsflyt, Taiga tilbyr et rikt, tilpasset miljø for å planlegge, spore og samarbeide med prosjektene dine, uten kompleksiteten av bedriftsverktøy eller leverandørens lås-in på SaaS-plattformene."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Test E2E Cli <https://example.com/>`__ is an application."
msgstr "`Test E2E Cli <https://example.com/>`__ Det er en søknad."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` resolves the caller's token through `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` and presents it as the Bearer"
msgstr "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` Løser oppkallerens token gjennom `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` og presentere det som Bearer"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Unit tests` verify isolated logic."
msgstr "`Unit tests` Sjekk isolert logikk."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`UsersLookup` yields the `no-reply` user dict used to derive `from` and `password`. Missing entries MUST yield an empty dict. The fallback for `from` is then `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."
msgstr "`UsersLookup` gir `no-reply` Brukerdikt brukt til å utlede `from` og `password`. Manglende poster må gi et tomt dikt. Rescue for `from` er da `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ is a powerful source code editor with a wide plugin ecosystem, supporting development workflows across many languages and platforms. See also the `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ and general `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ on Wikipedia."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ er en kraftig kildekode redaktør med et bredt plugin økosystem, støtte utvikling arbeidsflyter på mange språk og plattformer. Se også `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ og generelt `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ Wikipedia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://github.com/microsoft/vscode>`__ in a selectable flavor: the distribution’s Code - OSS build, VSCodium, or Microsoft’s own binary."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://github.com/microsoft/vscode>`__ i en utvalgbar smak: distribusjonens Code - OSS bygger, VSCodium eller Microsofts egen binær."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ is a versatile and widely used `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ that powers millions of websites, from blogs and portfolios to e-commerce and corporate sites. This deployment provides a containerized WordPress instance optimized for multisite operation, advanced media management, and extensive plugin support, allowing you to fully leverage the rich features of the WordPress software."
msgstr "`WordPress <https://en.wordpress.org/>`__ er en allsidig og mye brukt `content management system (CMS) <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_management_system>`__ som driver millioner av nettsteder, fra blogger og porteføljer til e-handel og selskapssider. Denne distribusjonen gir en beholderisert WordPress eksempel som er optimalisert for multisite drift, avansert mediestyring og omfattende plugin støtte, slik at du kan fullt ut utnytte de rike funksjonene i WordPress programvare."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ is an open-source helpdesk and ticketing system. Agents handle customer requests across email, chat, phone and web; customers can open tickets from a self-service portal."
msgstr "`Zammad <https://zammad.org/>`__ En åpen kildekilde helpdesk og billettsystem. Agenter håndterer kundeforespørsler på tvers av e-post, chat, telefon og web; kunder kan åpne billetter fra en selvbetjening portal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ is a popular video conferencing application for online meetings, webinars, and collaboration."
msgstr "`Zoom <https://zoom.us/>`__ er en populær videokonferansesøknad for online møter, webinarer og samarbeid."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → a device on the host, recovered over ssh then pulled; `[user@]host:/image` → the image is pulled and recovered locally (`device` / `full`)"
msgstr "`[user@]host:/dev/...` → en enhet på verten, gjenvunnet over ssh og deretter trukket; `[user@]host:/image` → bildet trekkes og gjenopprettes lokalt (`device` / `full`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`_as_bool` MUST accept the usual string forms (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), booleans, and numbers. Every boolean decision in the fallbacks MUST use it so that `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` values coming from YAML, environment variables, or already-coerced facts all behave the same."
msgstr "`_as_bool` Må akseptere vanlige strengskjemaer (`true|false|yes|no|1|0|on|off`), leveler og tall. Hver boolesk beslutning i tilbakefallene må bruke den slik at `SYSTEM_EMAIL_*` verdier som kommer fra YAML, miljøvariabler, eller allerede coerced fakta alle oppfører seg det samme."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`_compute` MUST delegate to three other lookup plugins rather than re-reading project state directly:"
msgstr "`_compute` Må delegere til tre andre oppslagsmoduler i stedet for å lese om prosjekttilstanden direkte:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`_shared.js` — env + login helpers (`penpotOidcLogin`, `penpotLdapLogin`, `penpotNativeLogin`, `penpotRegister`)."
msgstr "`_shared.js` — env + påloggingshjelpere (`penpotOidcLogin`, `penpotLdapLogin`, `penpotNativeLogin`, `penpotRegister`).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``\"block-above\"``: the construct's own line, or any comment line above it within the same blank-line-delimited block. A gettext entry stacks several comments and repeats a URL in both ``msgid`` and ``msgstr``, so a marker has to cover the whole entry and survive whichever writer appends its comment last."
msgstr "``\"block-above\"``: Konstruktørens egen linje, eller en kommentarlinje over den i samme blanklinjebegrenset blokk. En gettext-oppføring stabeler flere kommentarer og gjentar en URL i begge ``msgid`` og ``msgstr``, så en markør må dekke hele oppføringen og overleve som forfatter legger til sin kommentar sist."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``\"line-above\"``: marker must be on the immediately preceding non-empty line. Blank lines between marker and construct break the association."
msgstr "``\"line-above\"``: markøren må være på den umiddelbart foregående ikke-tom linje. Blanke linjer mellom markør og konstruksjon bryter foreningen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``\"same-line\"``: marker must be on the construct's line."
msgstr "``\"same-line\"``: Merkeren må være på konstruksjonens linje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``\"same-or-above\"`` (default): either of the above."
msgstr "``\"same-or-above\"`` (standard): En av de ovennevnte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``#`` (Python, YAML, shell, conf, INI, …)"
msgstr "``#`` (Python, YAML, skall, konf, INI, ...)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``#``, ``@``, ``+``, ``%`` and ``/`` introduce an axis and appear in neither a role id nor a display name, so the first of them is the seam."
msgstr "``#``, ``@``, ``+``, ``%`` og ``/`` introdusere en akse og vises ikke i en rolle-ID eller et visningsnavn, så den første av dem er sømmen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
