# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` erklærer a ``run-name:`` Det interpolerer forsendelsesinngangene. Når en kjøring er startet, er den tittelen den eneste rekorden av dem: REST API svar ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch Løp. Alt som ønsker å vite hva et løp ble sendt med derfor tolker tittelen - og tolker den mot et håndkopiert format ville drive det øyeblikket arbeidsflyten endres, stille og uten feil test."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` publiserer containerporten på en vertsportdockervalg, for en tjeneste adressert kun gjennom komponeringsnettverket."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` En eksplisitt per-service opt-in (standard feil) som gjør tjenesten tilgjengelig over nodeløken: dens havn får en dedikert ``HiddenServicePort``. Fordi ``applications`` er den variantmergede konfigurasjonen (base ``meta/services.yml`` Deep-merged med rundens ``meta/variants.yml`` overstyr)En tjeneste videresendes bare i varianten/konfigurasjonen der den setter ``exposed: true`` - som er akkurat det som lar de to DB varianter bli testet over Tor (v0 eksponert -> tilgjengelig, v1 ikke -> nektet).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: Hvem kan nå endepunktet?"

